<title>GERMANY: Wartime bombs hold up traffic at German airport.</title>
<headline>Wartime bombs hold up traffic at German airport.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flights were suspended for nearly an hour at Germany's Duesseldorf airport on Tuesday while experts defused two unexploded World War Two bombs found in the grounds, an airport spokesman said.</p>
<p>The two 500 kg (1,100 pound) bombs were found last week during excavation work at Germany's second largest airport.</p>
<p>Wolfgang Schieffers, head of the bomb disposal squad, said shrapnel could have flown in a 1,000-metre (yards) radius if the bombs had exploded. One flight was cancelled and 11 were delayed, but airport buildings were not evacuated.</p>
<p>Scores of unexploded World War Two bombs are still found in Germany every year.</p>
